Gas Flow Control - Operator Quick Guide
Release: v1.2
Web App: https://gas-flow-control-demo.web.app
 

Sign In
Use:
•	Authorized Harder employee email
•	Current 6-digit PIN
Only authorized personnel should have access.
Home Screen
The Home screen shows the overall system condition:
•	NORMAL - System operating normally
•	ADJUSTING - Valve moving to commanded position
•	WARNING - Condition requires attention
•	FAULT - Hardware/controller problem detected
•	OFFLINE / CONNECTION LOST - Controller communication unavailable
From Home, the operator can open:
•	Controls
•	Command History
•	Sign Out



Controls
Each controller/tool can display:
•	Tool number/name
•	Valve position
•	Gas flow
•	Pressure
•	Operating status
To adjust a valve:
1.	Select the correct tool.
2.	Enter the requested valve position.
3.	Confirm the command.
4.	Verify the displayed response.
0% = Closed
Valve Shutdown
Close Valve
Commands the selected valve to 0%.
Close All Valves
Commands all configured valves to 0%.
Always verify the displayed system response after issuing a shutdown command.




Command History
The History screen provides a record of recent valve commands, including tool, requested position, shutdown commands, and command results.
Offline Demo Mode
Demo Mode allows the interface to operate without Internet or physical valve hardware.
It can be used to demonstrate:
•	Login
•	Controls
•	Valve-position changes
•	Close Valve
•	Close All
•	Status behavior
•	Command History
Demo Mode does not control physical gas hardware.
Operator Reminders
•	Confirm the correct controller before sending a command.
•	Only operate controllers assigned to your work.
•	Do not rely on the app as the only means of physically isolating gas.
•	Continue to follow required manual shutoff and site safety procedures.
•	If the app reports FAULT, OFFLINE, or CONNECTION LOST, verify system condition before continuing.
•	Sign out when finished.

